MY PROJECTS

This repository contains my personal projects and technical documentation on Linux systems, web infrastructure, networking, cybersecurity, and software development.

PROJECTS

1. Repurposing My Old Phone into an ARM Linux Web Server

Repurposed an old Android smartphone into an ARM Linux web server.

The project covers unlocking the bootloader, flashing Linux images, installing and configuring Linux on the phone, and configuring the server so it can be accessed over SSH.

Focus: Linux, ARM, web servers, networking, system administration

Project:
https://www.sushantadk.com/Projects/repurposingMyOldPhone.html

2. Security Hardening and Assessment of a Self-Hosted ARM Alpine Linux Web Server

Security assessment and hardening of my self-hosted ARM Linux web server.

The project approaches the server from an attacker's perspective first, identifying exposed services and potential weaknesses before implementing security improvements.

Focus: Linux security, network security, firewall configuration, SSH, web server security, system hardening

Project:
https://www.sushantadk.com/Projects/hardeningTheServer.html

3. Numbers to Words Converter

A program that converts numerical values into their written-word representation.

This project demonstrates programming fundamentals, algorithm development, input handling, and integration of compiled software with a web application.

Focus: C++, algorithms, input processing, Flask integration

Project:
https://www.sushantadk.com/Projects/numbersToWords.html

4. Sunnyland

A 2D platform game developed using the Unity game engine.

The project explores game development concepts including gameplay programming, level design, player movement, and interactive game systems.

Focus: C#, Unity, game development

Project:
https://www.sushantadk.com/Projects/sunnyland.html

SUPPORTING DOCUMENTS

The following documents describe infrastructure and engineering work associated with my projects.

1. Initial Configuration of My Website

Documentation of the initial creation and organization of my website, including the structure of its HTML pages and supporting files.

Focus: HTML, website structure, file organization

Documentation:
